comments.body:
 @MilosKozak 
Beta 11 crashs immediately after start for me on Pixel 6 (December 21 Update) with DanaRS. Beta 9 no problems at all.

I see a warning "Application needs bluetooth permission" and then the application crashs. All possible permissions have been given (see screenshot).

![permissions](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7951225/146274120-29db296e-18c5-44f6-a760-80663fa777b1.png)

[crash.log](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7723075/crash.log)

// Edit: After crashing 50 times in a row it now works. No more Error regarding needing bluetooth permission. The check seems to be bugged?

@tanja3981 did you try to clear all data from AAPS and also from bluetooth system app?
I also recommend a reboot after that.
Then AAPS should start with the new installation wizard.
